<div class="mt-10" id="topic-elements-of-propositional-logic">

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">
        2. Elements of Propositional Logic
    </h2>

    <div class="w-full h-[1px] flex items-center justify-center pt-[10px]">
        <div class="bg-gray-600 w-full h-[1px]"></div>
    </div>

    <p class="text-md text-gray-400 px-3 mt-3 leading-relaxed">The basic elements used in propositional logic are propositions, truth values, and logical connectives.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mt-4"><table class="w-full border-collapse"><thead><tr class="border-b border-[#3A2560] text-white"><th class="p-3">Element</th><th class="p-3">Description</th><th class="p-3">Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="border-b border-[#3A2560]"><td class="p-3 text-white">Proposition</td><td class="p-3">A declarative statement with a definite truth value.</td><td class="p-3">“7 is prime.”</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-[#3A2560]"><td class="p-3 text-white">Truth value</td><td class="p-3">Indicates whether a proposition is true (T) or false (F).</td><td class="p-3">“7 is prime” has value T.</td></tr><tr><td class="p-3 text-white">Logical connective</td><td class="p-3">Combines propositions or changes a proposition's truth value.</td><td class="p-3">\(p \land q\)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-6">Simple and Compound Propositions</h3><p class="text-md text-gray-400 px-3 mt-3 leading-relaxed">A <strong class="text-white">simple proposition</strong> expresses one statement without a logical connective. A <strong class="text-white">compound proposition</strong> is formed by combining or modifying propositions using connectives.</p>
<div class="bg-[#1B0D2D] border border-[#3A2560] rounded-lg p-5 space-y-3"><p class="text-md text-gray-400 px-3 mt-3 leading-relaxed"><span class="text-white font-semibold">Simple:</span> \(p\): “The library is open.”</p><p class="text-md text-gray-400 px-3 mt-3 leading-relaxed"><span class="text-white font-semibold">Simple:</span> \(q\): “I have a library card.”</p><p class="text-md text-gray-400 px-3 mt-3 leading-relaxed"><span class="text-white font-semibold">Compound:</span> \(p \land q\): “The library is open and I have a library card.”</p></div><p class="text-md text-gray-400 px-3 mt-3 leading-relaxed">When evaluating a compound proposition, determine the truth values of its component propositions first, then apply the connective's rule.</p>
</div>
